      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The privacy and bias arguments are absolutely legitimate and represent the most significant political and legal hurdles for this technology right now.\n\nBias is a real issue because some AI models are trained on biased data, leading to higher misidentification rates for certain demographics, which can cause unjust targeting. Privacy is a major legal challenge because the comprehensive, always-on collection of personal biometric data fundamentally changes the relationship between the government and the citizen, leading to strong opposition from civil liberty advocates globally.",
      "source": "target",
